msgid "Mg過剰"
msgstr "Mg-rich"

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:331
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"O過剰からMg過剰へ条件を移すと、酸素空孔の形成エネルギーは6.2 eV下がり、Mg空孔の形成エネルギーは 同じだけ上がる（:numref"
":`fig-defect-formation-dependence`\\ の左）。同じ構造・同じ計算条件の :math:`E_{\\rm "
"f}^0` を使っても、化学ポテンシャルの選び方だけで値が eV の単位で変わる。 一方、2つの空孔の和 :math:`E_{\\rm "
"f}[V_{\\rm O}]+E_{\\rm f}[V_{\\rm Mg}]=E_{\\rm f}^0[V_{\\rm O}]+E_{\\rm "
"f}^0[V_{\\rm Mg}]+\\Delta H_{\\rm f}` は "
"化学ポテンシャルによらない。2つの空孔で取り除いた原子がMgOの化学量論の比（Mg 1個とO 1個）になり、 :eq:`defect-"
"compound-equilibrium`\\ により :math:`\\Delta\\mu_{\\rm "
"Mg}+\\Delta\\mu_{\\rm O}=\\Delta H_{\\rm f}` が "
"一定だからである。この和は、離れた位置に別々に作った2つの中性の空孔の値を足したものである。 "
"陽イオンと陰イオンの空孔の組（Schottky欠陥）の実際の形成エネルギーには、各空孔の電荷状態と、 "
"近くにある空孔どうしの結合が関わるので、この和とは一般に異なる。"
msgstr ""
"Moving from O-rich to Mg-rich conditions lowers the oxygen vacancy "
"formation energy by 6.2 eV and raises the Mg vacancy formation energy by "
"the same amount (left panel of :numref:`fig-defect-formation-"
"dependence`\\ ). Even using :math:`E_{\\rm f}^0` for the same structure "
"and calculation settings, changing the chemical potentials alone shifts "
"the values by several eV. By contrast, the sum for the two vacancies, "
":math:`E_{\\rm f}[V_{\\rm O}]+E_{\\rm f}[V_{\\rm Mg}]=E_{\\rm "
"f}^0[V_{\\rm O}]+E_{\\rm f}^0[V_{\\rm Mg}]+\\Delta H_{\\rm f}`, is "
"independent of the chemical potentials. The removed atoms are in the "
"stoichiometric ratio of MgO (one Mg and one O), so Equation :eq:`defect-"
"compound-equilibrium`\\  fixes :math:`\\Delta\\mu_{\\rm "
"Mg}+\\Delta\\mu_{\\rm O}=\\Delta H_{\\rm f}`. This sum is for two neutral"
" vacancies formed separately at sites far apart. The actual formation "
"energy of a cation–anion vacancy pair (Schottky defect) depends on the "
"charge states of the vacancies and on their binding at short separation, "
"so it generally differs from this sum."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:341
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**荷電欠陥の模型。** バンドギャップ3.0 eVの物質で、:math:`E_{\\rm F}=0` での形成エネルギーが 電荷 "
":math:`+1`、0、:math:`-1` に対してそれぞれ1.0、1.8、3.4 eVの欠陥を考える （値は説明のための仮定）。:eq"
":`defect-transition-level`\\ から "
":math:`\\varepsilon(+1/0)=(1.0-1.8)/(0-1)=0.8` "
"eV、:math:`\\varepsilon(0/{-1})=(1.8-3.4)/(-1-0)=1.6` eVである。 :numref:`fig-"
"defect-formation-dependence`\\ の右で、太線は各フェルミ準位で最も低い形成エネルギーを つないだもので、0.8 "
"eVより下では電荷 :math:`+1`、0.8〜1.6 eVでは中性、1.6 eVより上では 電荷 :math:`-1` が安定である。"
msgstr ""
"**Charged-defect model.** Consider a defect in a material with a band gap"
" of 3.0 eV. At :math:`E_{\\rm F}=0`, assume formation energies of 1.0, "
"1.8, and 3.4 eV for charges :math:`+1`, 0, and :math:`-1`, respectively, "
"for illustration. Equation :eq:`defect-transition-level`\\  gives "
":math:`\\varepsilon(+1/0)=(1.0-1.8)/(0-1)=0.8` eV and "
":math:`\\varepsilon(0/{-1})=(1.8-3.4)/(-1-0)=1.6` eV. In the right panel "
"of :numref:`fig-defect-formation-dependence`\\ , the thick line connects "
"the minimum formation energies at each Fermi level. The stable charge "
"state is :math:`+1` below 0.8 eV, neutral from 0.8 to 1.6 eV, and "
":math:`-1` above 1.6 eV."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:349
msgid "左は酸素の化学ポテンシャルに対して、酸素空孔の形成エネルギーが上がり、Mg空孔の形成エネルギーが下がる2本の直線。右はフェルミ準位に対する3つの電荷状態の形成エネルギーと、その最小値をつないだ折れ線。"
msgstr ""
"The left panel shows two lines. As the oxygen chemical potential "
"increases, the oxygen vacancy formation energy rises and the Mg vacancy "
"formation energy falls. The right panel shows the formation energies for "
"three charge states versus the Fermi level, with a piecewise linear curve"
" tracing their minimum."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:354
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"左：MgOの酸素空孔（実線）とMg空孔（破線）の形成エネルギーの変化\\ :eq:`defect-mgo-vacancies`\\ 。 "
"縦軸は、取り除いた元素の単体と平衡な条件（:math:`\\Delta\\mu=0`）での値 :math:`E_{\\rm f}^0` からの差。"
" 点線は2つの変化の和で、:math:`\\Delta H_{\\rm f}=-6.235` eVで一定。 "
"右：仮定した荷電欠陥の形成エネルギー\\ :eq:`defect-formation-charged`\\ 。細線は電荷 :math:`+1`\\"
" （破線）、 0（一点鎖線）、:math:`-1`\\ （点線）、太線は最小値、黒丸は遷移準位。"
msgstr ""
"The left panel shows the change in formation energy for an oxygen vacancy"
" (solid line) and an Mg vacancy (dashed line) in MgO, from Equation \\ "
":eq:`defect-mgo-vacancies`\\ . The vertical axis shows the difference "
"from the value at equilibrium with the elemental phase of the removed "
"element (:math:`\\Delta\\mu=0`). That value is :math:`E_{\\rm f}^0`. The "
"dotted line is the sum of the two changes and is constant at "
":math:`\\Delta H_{\\rm f}=-6.235` eV. The right panel shows the formation"
" energies in the charged-defect model, from Equation \\ :eq:`defect-"
"formation-charged`\\ . Thin lines show charge :math:`+1`\\  (dashed), "
"charge 0 (dash-dotted), and charge :math:`-1`\\  (dotted). The thick line"
" shows the minimum formation energy, and the black dots mark the "
"transition levels."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:360
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**欠陥濃度。** :eq:`defect-concentration`\\ で :math:`S_{\\rm "
"f}=0`、:math:`E_{\\rm f}=1.0` eVとすると、 濃度は300 Kで "
":math:`1.6\\times10^{-17}`、600 Kで :math:`4.0\\times10^{-9}`、1000 Kで "
":math:`9.1\\times10^{-6}` である。 :eq:`defect-gibbs-derivative`\\ から得た "
":math:`n/(N-n)=\\exp(-E_{\\rm f}/k_{\\rm B}T)` を厳密に :math:`n/N` "
"へ直しても、この3つの値は表示した桁では変わらない。300 Kでは形成エネルギーが0.1 eV下がるだけで "
"濃度が約48倍になる。上のMgOのように化学ポテンシャルで形成エネルギーが数eV変わると、 濃度は何十けたも変わりうる。"
msgstr ""
"**Defect concentration.** Equation :eq:`defect-concentration`\\  with "
":math:`S_{\\rm f}=0` and :math:`E_{\\rm f}=1.0` eV gives concentrations "
"of :math:`1.6\\times10^{-17}` at 300 K, :math:`4.0\\times10^{-9}` at 600 "
"K, and :math:`9.1\\times10^{-6}` at 1000 K. Even converting the ratio "
"from Equation :eq:`defect-gibbs-derivative`\\ , "
":math:`n/(N-n)=\\exp(-E_{\\rm f}/k_{\\rm B}T)`, to the exact fraction "
":math:`n/N` leaves these three values unchanged at the displayed "
"precision. At 300 K, a drop in formation energy of just 0.1 eV increases "
"the concentration by about a factor of 48. If the chemical potentials "
"change the formation energy by several eV, as in the MgO example, the "
"concentration can change by tens of orders of magnitude."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:370
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:372
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**化学ポテンシャルの基準。** 形成エネルギーの値は、:math:`\\mu_i` をどの条件で選んだかと一緒に示して "
"初めて意味をもつ。共通の参照 :math:`E_i^{\\rm ref}` と計算条件のもとでリザーバーの条件だけが違う値どうしは、 :eq"
":`defect-formation-delta-mu`\\ の第2項の差だけずれる。手法が違う値どうしでは、:math:`E_{\\rm "
"f}^0` と :math:`\\mu_i` の両方が違いうる。例えば\\ `Li₃PO₄のLi空孔形成エネルギー "
"<https://example.quloud-platform.quemix.com/li3po4/vacancy-"
"formation.html>`__\\ では、 Li\\ :sub:`3`\\ PO\\ :sub:`4`\\ "
"の32原子の不規則構造からLiを1個取り除いた形成エネルギーが、 文献のDFTでは約5 eV、事例のOpenMXでは約3〜4 "
"eVである。2つの計算は元の原子配置も異なる。この差を手法の精度の差として読むには、 "
"構造、Liの化学ポテンシャル、緩和の条件をそろえる必要がある。どの要因がどれだけ効いているかは、 条件をそろえた計算なしには決められない。"
msgstr ""
"**Chemical potential references.** A formation energy is meaningful only "
"when reported together with the conditions used to choose :math:`\\mu_i`."
" With a common reference :math:`E_i^{\\rm ref}` and the same calculation "
"settings, formation energies that differ only in reservoir conditions "
"differ by the change in the second term of Equation :eq:`defect-"
"formation-delta-mu`\\ . When the methods differ, both :math:`E_{\\rm "
"f}^0` and :math:`\\mu_i` can differ. The calculation example \\ `Li "
"Vacancy Formation Energy in Li₃PO₄ <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/li3po4/vacancy-formation.html>`__\\  discusses "
"removal of one Li atom from a 32-atom disordered Li\\ :sub:`3`\\ PO\\ "
":sub:`4`\\  structure. The formation energy is about 5 eV in the "
"published DFT calculation and about 3–4 eV in the OpenMX example. The two"
" calculations also start from different atomic configurations. To "
"interpret the difference as a difference in method accuracy, use the same"
" structure, Li chemical potential, and relaxation conditions. Without "
"calculations under matching conditions, the contribution of each factor "
"cannot be determined."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:380
msgid ""
"**スーパーセルの大きさ。** 欠陥はその周期像と、ひずみ場（距離の3乗に反比例して弱まる）や、 荷電欠陥では静電相互作用（:eq"
":`defect-makov-payne`\\ のように距離に反比例）を通じて相互作用する。 "
"セルを大きくして形成エネルギーの変化を調べると、孤立した欠陥の値にどれだけ近いかが分かる。"
msgstr ""
"**Supercell size.** A defect interacts with its periodic images through "
"strain fields, which decay as the inverse cube of the distance, and for "
"charged defects through electrostatic interactions, which decay inversely"
" with distance as in Equation :eq:`defect-makov-payne`\\ . Increasing the"
" cell size and checking the change in formation energy shows how close it"
" is to the isolated-defect value."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:383
msgid ""
"**緩和と構造。** 欠陥のまわりの緩和には複数の極小がありうる。初期構造によって異なる極小に "
"落ちると、同じ欠陥でも形成エネルギーが変わる。非晶質では、取り除くサイトごとに環境が違うので、 形成エネルギーは1つの値ではなく分布になる。"
msgstr ""
"**Relaxation and structure.** Relaxation around a defect can lead to more"
" than one minimum. If the starting structures relax to different minima, "
"the formation energy can differ even for the same defect. In amorphous "
"solids, the local environment differs with the site from which the atom "
"is removed, so the formation energy has a distribution rather than a "
"single value."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:386
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**エネルギーの精度。** GGAなどの近似汎関数はO\\ :sub:`2`\\ 分子の結合を過大に見積もり、 "
"酸化物の生成エネルギーに系統的な誤差を生む [DefWang2006]_。バンドギャップを小さく見積もると、 "
"荷電欠陥でフェルミ準位を動かせる範囲と遷移準位の位置も変わる。機械学習ポテンシャルで形成エネルギーを "
"求める場合も、:math:`E_i^{\\rm ref}` を同じモデルで求めないと、基準のずれが相殺しない。"
msgstr ""
"**Energy accuracy.** Approximate functionals such as GGA overestimate "
"binding in O\\ :sub:`2`\\  molecules, introducing systematic errors in "
"oxide formation energies [DefWang2006]_. Underestimating the band gap "
"also changes the range over which the Fermi level can vary for charged "
"defects and the positions of the transition levels. When a machine "
"learning potential is used to calculate formation energies, use the same "
"model to obtain :math:`E_i^{\\rm ref}` so that the reference offsets "
"cancel."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:390
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**有限温度。** :eq:`defect-formation-neutral`\\ は絶対零度の全エネルギーで書いた。高温では、 "
"振動のエントロピー :math:`S_{\\rm f}` と、気相などのリザーバーの化学ポテンシャルの温度依存性が効く。"
msgstr ""
"**Finite temperature.** Equation :eq:`defect-formation-neutral`\\  uses "
"total energies at absolute zero. At high temperatures, the vibrational "
"entropy :math:`S_{\\rm f}` and the temperature dependence of the chemical"
" potentials of reservoirs such as gases affect the result."

#: ../../electronic/defect_formation.rst:392
msgid ""
"**空孔の数を固定したモデル。** 欠陥濃度の節で述べたように、空孔を人為的に入れたモデルの拡散の温度依存性には、 "
"空孔を熱平衡で生成する寄与が入らない。実験の試料で空孔が熱平衡で生成されるなら、実験の拡散の温度依存性には "
"この寄与が含まれ、組成や不純物で空孔の数が決まっているなら含まれない。どちらの場合かで、モデルの値と比べてよい量が変わる。空孔の割合が拡散係数の値そのものに効くことは、"
" \\ :ref:`平均二乗変位と拡散係数の解釈と限界<msd-interpretation-limits>`\\ で述べる。"
msgstr ""
"**Models with a fixed number of vacancies.** As described in the section "
"on defect concentration, the temperature dependence of diffusion in a "
"model with manually inserted vacancies excludes vacancy formation at "
"thermal equilibrium. If vacancies form at thermal equilibrium in the "
"experimental sample, the temperature dependence of diffusion in that "
"sample includes this contribution. If the number of vacancies is set by "
"the composition or impurities, it does not. Which case applies determines"
" the quantity that can be compared with the model. The section on \\ "
":ref:`interpretation and limitations of the mean squared displacement and"
" diffusion coefficient <msd-interpretation-limits>`\\  explains how the "
"vacancy fraction affects the value of the diffusion coefficient itself."

